# Wave W17-T (Route 133): rapid sand — rapid-edge sand: a paler, cooler shore sand at the middle current\u2019s edge, its foam flecks harder and denser than the first road\u2019s — short bright dashes standing thick in the tread, the faster water combing the shore harder (design: the middle road, faster than the first, its surface tilting everything eastward; the shipped current cells are mechanic data, byte-identical entire). Route 133\u2019s own sand — the hardest-foamed of the three current shores: split from Route 132\u2019s stream sand by foam density and temperature (cool, hard dashes vs warm, loose streaks) and from Route 134\u2019s gate sand by register (rapid edge vs delivery channel).
